+// The rain's rings on the water (`look::weather`, benilla's own): in cells of about two-thirds of a
+// yard, three offset layers, a drop lands in a share of the cells (`amount`, the rain) and its ring
+// spreads and fades over about two-thirds of a second, each cell on its own beat. Returns the
+// slope (x, z) the rings add to the surface; zero far off, where a ring is under a pixel.
+fn rain_hash3(c: vec2<f32>) -> vec3<f32> {
+    let q = vec3<f32>(dot(c, vec2<f32>(127.1, 311.7)), dot(c, vec2<f32>(269.5, 183.3)), dot(c, vec2<f32>(419.2, 371.9)));
